WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:05.240
What's up guys I'm Colin for theScore esports. Professional League of Legends

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.340
has been around since mid 2010 and since then we've seen some incredible rosters

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:16.560
rise and fall. Now the question is which of those squads reigns supreme in the

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.720
history of League of Legends. It is a tough question to answer but one we here at

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:26.570
theScore esports were up to taking on. We took into account regional dominance,

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:31.700
international performance and yes impact on a given era to come up with

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:37.740
our list of the Top 10 Most Dominant League of Legends Rosters of All Time.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:45.160
Coming in at number 10 is a 2013 Cloud9 squad that burst onto the North American LCS scene

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.680
and changed the way that that that region played League of Legends.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:56.620
Balls, Meteos, Hai, Sneaky and LemonNation dominated their first LCS split,

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:02.360
fielding a 25-3 record en route to an LCS title.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:26.360
(Casting)

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:35.220
After that impressive first split, this lineup went on to win another NA LCS title in the 2014 spring split

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:41.160
as well as back-to-back Worlds berths in 2013 and 2014.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.700
At number nine we have Fnatic’s dominant 2015 roster

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:53.380
that saw the likes of Huni, Reignover, Febiven, Rekkles and YellowStar

00:01:53.500 --> 00:02:00.260
make history as the only European team to go undefeated for an entire regular season.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:03.860
(Casting)

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:08.140
(Casting)

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:13.880
(Casting)

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:21.900
(Casting)

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.660
(Casting)

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.980
Many have called this team the best roster the west has ever produced.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:40.260
Their perfect 18-0 record throughout the 2015 summer split translated into yet another EU LCS championship.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:45.660
and the team would then go on to become one of the first Western rosters to ever finish

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.040
in the Top 4 at Worlds.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:54.380
At number eight are the reigning world champions, Samsung Galaxy.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:03:00.920
Samsung may have not been heralded as the best Korean roster heading into Worlds 2017

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:03.920
but that’s what made their victory so special.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:12.200
Cuvee, Ambition, Crown, Ruler and CoreJJ surprised the entire world by doing something that had never been

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:12.760
done

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:16.740
beating Faker in a Worlds finals.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:51.680
(Casting)

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:54.880
The team not only beat SK Telecom in the finals,

00:03:54.880 --> 00:04:00.900
but swept the series in three consecutive games, cementing their place in history.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:08.520
Our number seven team is the 2015 edition of China’s Edward Gaming.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:14.920
This veteran squad consisted of Koro1, Clearlove, PawN, Deft and Meiko

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:21.160
and became the first non-Korean team to win a major international event in the LCS era

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:25.720
when they defeated SKT in the finals of MSI in 2015.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:51.000
(Casting)

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:58.560
Their MSI victory aside, this roster dominated the LPL, winning back-to-back LPL splits.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:05.420
Coming in at number 6 is Korean powerhouse Kingzone DragonX.

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:14.540
In 2018, the roster consisting of Khan, Peanut, Bdd, Pray and GorillA put up a whopping 16-2 record

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:20.820
in the LCK and continued that momentum into the playoffs en route to an LCK title.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:30.420
(Casting)

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:49.800
(Casting)

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:56.400
During that season, members of Kingzone made up 4 of the top 10 KDA rankings in the region.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:00.940
This roster is the consensus best team on the planet right now,

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:06.000
and they are the odds on favorite to take home this year’s MSI title.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:12.600
Before the LCS was formed, competitive League of Legends was very different

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:17.560
and nobody embodied this unique style  more than Moscow 5.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:21.220
In an era where everyone was trying to stall out the game,

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:28.060
Darien, Diamondprox, Alex Ich, Genja and GosuPepper ran right down their enemies’ throats

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:31.100
and closed out games in under 30 minutes

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:35.340
"And this was their era, this was when they had the most vitality and the most force the most impact.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:38.720
on the game. And they were the best team in the world. They were dominating.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:43.220
Like when I first saw them at those first IEMs. They were getting wins in 20 minutes.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:47.080
Even against the best teams in the world. They were making teams just look embarrassing.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:50.020
(Casting)

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:53.220
(Casting)

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:57.280
(Casting)

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:00.760
(Casting)

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:04.270
(Casting)

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:09.140
(Casting)

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:13.340
(Casting)

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:18.000
(Casting)

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:23.140
(Casting)

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:28.740
During their reign of terror in 2012, they won the IEM season 6 world championship

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:34.020
and IEM Kiev in addition to 11 other tournaments.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:43.480
At number four we’ve got the 2016 edition of the ROX Tigers. Sure, Smeb, Peanut, Kuro, Pray and GorillA

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:50.900
ultimately played second fiddle to SKT, but the Tigers put up some of the most impressive results we’ve ever seen.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:59.380
ROX were finished first overall even above SKT in both the 2016 spring and summer split regular seasons,

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.340
bringing home the LCK title in Summer.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:05.740
(Casting)

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:12.220
(Casting)

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:17.470
(Casting)

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:25.080
(Casting)

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:33.260
(Casting)

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:37.480
Despite the fact that they were never able to win a major international title

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:42.520
Pray, GorillA and company deserve to be considered among the game’s best.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:49.260
At number three we’ve got SK Telecom T1K, and let’s be honest

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.240
you knew it was coming.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:57.680
In 2013 SKT won the Season 3 World Championship with Faker in the mid lane,

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:04.420
Impact in the top lane, Bengi in the Jungle, Piglet at ADC and PoohManDu at Support.

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:08.480
They beat the KT Rolster Bullets to bring home the Korean regional title

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:11.760
and then set their eyes on the World Championship.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:38.040
(Casting)

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:44.520
Their Worlds victory and 15-3 combined record at the event was truly a turning point in

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:50.760
pro League that led to the era of SKT dominance we know so well today.

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:55.540
At number two we have the team that put up the most convincing

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:58.920
world championship performance the game has ever seen

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:00.760
Samsung White.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:07.500
Looper, Dandy, PawN, Imp and Mata made up one of the strongest lineups in the game’s history

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:13.280
and they battled hard with Samsung Blue during championship summer 2014 in Korea

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.620
but ultimately finished 3rd.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:19.120
But, when it came to Worlds they were able to settle into the patch

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:22.340
and their hyper aggressive play and incredible vision control

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:26.040
made them unstoppable on the game’s biggest stage.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:31.600
"They come into the series as the heavy favourites. And we've seen them absolutely dominate the competition

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:32.380
throughout Worlds."

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:36.000
"And to say that Samsung White has been dominant is absolutely an understatement."

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:40.060
"They've taken out the number one Chinese, North American, and Korean seeds

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.840
throughout this entire tournament only dropping a single game."

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:47.740
(Casting)

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:52.360
(Casting)

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:55.300
(Casting)

00:10:55.300 --> 00:11:00.540
(Casting)

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:11.120
(Casting)

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:18.560
Coming in at number one is the best of all of SKT’s dominant lineups.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:24.580
The core of Faker, Wolf, Bang, Bengi have collected the most impressive body of work

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:27.400
in the history of League of Legends.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:32.040
This team won the World Championship in 2015 with MaRin in the top lane,

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:36.840
as well as both the spring and summer LCK playoffs that year.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:43.400
That same core was able to do it all again in 2016 with the addition of Duke over MaRin

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:47.160
in the top lane and Blank as a secondary jungler.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:12:11.080
(Casting)

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:17.080
The organization was unstoppable and set the bar for what it means to dominate.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:22.700
Okay guys, that's out list. Now if your favourite League of Legends roster did not make the cut.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:26.760
Feel free to make your case in the comments below, and I will see you next week.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:32.500
Thanks for watching. If you want more great content just like this, be sure to hit the subscribe button.

